# Deep-Guard Fix — 2026-07-10T20:08:33+03:30
# File: /tmp/dvna/core/appHandler.js  Line: 235  Severity: critical
# Type: crypto_issue

## Root Cause
The use of external entity processing can lead to XML External Entity (XXE) attacks, allowing attackers to access internal files or systems.

## Explanation
The patch disables external entity processing by setting the 'noent' option to false when parsing the XML. This prevents potential XXE attacks, ensuring that only the intended XML content is processed without exposing sensitive data or internal resources.

## Patch
--- a/tmp/dvna/core/appHandler.js
+++ b/tmp/dvna/core/appHandler.js
@@ -235,7 +235,7 @@
 var products = libxmljs.parseXmlString(req.files.products.data.toString('utf8'), {noent:true,noblanks:true})
+var products = libxmljs.parseXmlString(req.files.products.data.toString('utf8'), {noent:false,noblanks:true})
 
